# Structural backstop against edge HTML rewriting.
#
# Cloudflare's Email Address Obfuscation documentation states obfuscation does
# not occur when Cache-Control: no-transform is set — that part is primary
# source. The equivalent claim for Real User Monitoring beacon injection is
# NOT firmly established, so this file is a second layer, never the primary
# control. The primary controls are the dashboard toggles and the Configuration
# Rule; this only narrows the window if one of those silently fails.
#
# Scoped to the HTML files only. Whether no-transform also suppresses
# Cloudflare's Brotli/gzip re-compression is unverified, and there is no reason
# to risk that on the CSS and the images.

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, no-transform
/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, no-transform
/privacy.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, no-transform
/support.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, no-transform
/404.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, no-transform

# Cloudflare attaches a Network Error Logging policy that GitHub Pages never
# sent, pointing the browser at https://a.nel.cloudflare.com/report/v4 — a
# third-party origin. It only fires on failed requests (success_fraction 0.0)
# and is not a "loaded resource", so it does not falsify the privacy page's
# wording, but it is a data flow we did not choose and did not disclose.
# max_age 0 instructs the browser to discard the policy. Whether this override
# actually lands is verified on the wire after deploy, not assumed.

/*
  NEL: {"max_age":0}

